  "encounterTable": "route_1",
  "_design": "A ring, not a fork, and the ring bends eight times, because a loop drawn as a rectangle reads as a racetrack round a lawn. The road out of Hearthmere jogs east, crosses the burn on the only plank on the map, jogs back and reaches a junction at y22. From there a west lane (x6-7) and an east lane (x31-32) go round and rejoin on the cross road at y8, and the spine carries on to Briarbell through a gap in the march fence. Everything worth finding is INSIDE the ring -- the fenced hay field, the tarn, the long grass -- so a player who guesses wrong at the junction loses nothing but time, and a player who walks the whole ring has seen the route. The burn is the one hard line across the map: gate meadow below it, ring above.",
  "_plan": "Meadow, light woodland, a burn, wooden fences, gentle rises: the safest road in Caelora, and the one that has to teach everything. The first long grass is a planted patch beside the gate. The first trainer stands north of the plank, which is the only crossing, so she cannot be walked past -- but far enough up that the player has waded some grass and picked something up first. Gathering is four pickups lying in plain sight and two buried ones, and two of the four sit across water and cannot be had until the player can wade, which is this route's reason to come back. The fences do most of the reading: a rectangle of long grass with a rail round it and a gate in the bottom is a hay field; the same rectangle without the rail is scenery.",
